==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|Cambogia||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|fr|Cambodge}} and {{der|en|pt|Camboja}}. Both words are derived from {{w|Middle Khmer}} ''Kambuja'' (Modern {{der|en|km|កម្ពុជា}}). Ultimately from {{der|en|sa|काम्बोज|pos=the name of a tribe mentioned in Hindu scripture}}. {{doublet|en|Kampuchea|gamboge}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|[kæmˈboʊdi.ə]}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-Cambodia.ogg|a=US}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{senseid|en|Q424}}{{place|en|country|r/Southeast Asia|official=Kingdom of Cambodia|capital=Phnom Penh}}. Former name: [[Kampuchea]].

